we have ProductRepository interface on domain that is not extended to "JpaRepository"!
we have ProductJpaRepository interface on persistence package that is extended to "JpaRepository"
(so it is our real repo)


we have ProductRepositoryAdapter class that connect this to interface,
by this design we never use our db detail on domain area
this is dependency inversion!


HEXAGONAL ARCHITECTURE
This is "Hexagonal Architecture"
the domain declares what it needs
("give me invoices by public token", "give me the next number") without knowing how

It is called:
Ports and Adapters

Port
An interface defined by the domain.

Adapter
The concrete implementation of that interface.

Note: It is called Hexagonal Architecture because of the diagram shape,
      not because the system must have exactly six parts.
      the core application/domain is in the center
      it can connect to the outside world from multiple sides
      those connections happen through ports
      the external tools are adapters
      So “hexagonal” is mostly a visual metaphor for a system with a central core and multiple external connections.